<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:56:55 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>France marks 10 years since Bastille Day terror attack in Nice killed 86</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-france-marks-10-years-since-bastille-day-terror-attack-in-nice-killed-86</link><description>
Religious leaders have gathered in Nice for an interfaith service to pray for the victims of the Bastille Day terror attack, on the eve of the 10th anniversary of the atrocity that killed 86 people and injured more than 400. President Emmanuel Macron is due to lead the main memorial ceremony later on Tuesday, while a minute's silence will be observed before France's World Cup semi-final against Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa8e1a84-7e98-11f1-83f4-efef7f7c984b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:12:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg">AFP - VALERY HACHE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fifty-nine arrested over wildfires, including Fontainebleau blaze near Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-france-fifty-nine-arrested-over-wildfires-two-for-fontainebleau-forest-blaze-near-paris</link><description>
A total of 59 people have been arrested across France over suspected deliberate or accidental arson, including two in connection with the wildfire still sweeping through the Fontainebleau forest southeast of Paris, Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez has said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6a01b0a-7f54-11f1-ae18-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T221512Z-683314971-RC29DMA8SHKN-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6a01b0a-7f54-11f1-ae18-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T221512Z-683314971-RC29DMA8SHKN-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11f26780-7f4c-11f1-b471-b182ab756299</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 06:22:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6a01b0a-7f54-11f1-ae18-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T221512Z-683314971-RC29DMA8SHKN-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">REUTERS - Stephane Mahe</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine's allies pledge jets, missiles and anti-ballistic shield at Paris summit</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260714-ukraine-s-allies-pledge-jets-missiles-and-anti-ballistic-shield-at-paris-summit</link><description>
Ukraine's allies announced additional air defence support for Kyiv at a summit in Paris on Monday, along with exercises for the forces that will be deployed after a ceasefire, as part of efforts to increase pressure on Russia to end the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf21afce-7f01-11f1-af6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T163612Z-1269730039-RC24DMAN3E13-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-COALITION-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf21afce-7f01-11f1-af6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T163612Z-1269730039-RC24DMAN3E13-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-COALITION-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3fd490d0-7f5e-11f1-b426-45e43ba2eff1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 09:40:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf21afce-7f01-11f1-af6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T163612Z-1269730039-RC24DMAN3E13-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-COALITION-FRANCE.jpg">via REUTERS - Teresa Suarez</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France, Spain collide for World Cup final berth with Deschamps chasing history</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260713-france-and-spain-prepare-to-duel-at-world-cup</link><description>
France's attack led by Kylian Mbappe take on a technically accomplished Spain team in the first semi-final of the World Cup on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fbe41f6e-7f29-11f1-9f6a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e71a1954bfe843fd704640133a6a1de1dfc3fbf1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fbe41f6e-7f29-11f1-9f6a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e71a1954bfe843fd704640133a6a1de1dfc3fbf1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42ee3636-7eff-11f1-877b-3b41530b611d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:10:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fbe41f6e-7f29-11f1-9f6a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/e71a1954bfe843fd704640133a6a1de1dfc3fbf1.jpg">© FRANCK FIFE / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris balls cancelled amid heatwave as France marks 10 years since Nice attack</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260713-bastille-day-events-disrupted-by-heat-as-france-marks-nice-attack-anniversary</link><description>
Bastille Day firefighters' balls in Paris and the surrounding suburbs have been cancelled owing to record high temperatures affecting the capital and most of France, as emergency workers remain on alert. Celebrations begin on Monday, with Paris having brought forward its annual fireworks display by a day to avoid clashing with commemorations marking the 10th anniversary of the Nice attack of 14 July, 2016.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e326d98-7eb5-11f1-8c6f-fb9125324903</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:25:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France, Germany, UK condemn Iran attacks as renewed fighting with US puts peace deal at risk</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-france-germany-uk-condemn-iran-attacks-as-renewed-fighting-with-us-puts-peace-deal-at-risk</link><description>
The foreign ministers of France, Germany, and Britain have condemned Iran's attacks on shipping in the Strait of Hormuz and on countries in the region, as Iran and the United States have traded attacks in recent days, casting doubt on their interim agreement to end the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ec205ec-7ea5-11f1-bf7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T053825Z-34279053-RC2ORKA8YMAI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-JET-FUEL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ec205ec-7ea5-11f1-bf7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T053825Z-34279053-RC2ORKA8YMAI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-JET-FUEL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44770c08-7ec8-11f1-a564-dbb701fa6098</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:47:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ec205ec-7ea5-11f1-bf7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T053825Z-34279053-RC2ORKA8YMAI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-JET-FUEL.jpg">© Retuers</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Mbappé, Dembélé, Olise dazzle up front but Maignan makes it possible</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260713-maignan-keeps-it-tight-at-the-back-as-france-s-fun-boy-three-make-hay-up-front-world-cup-2026</link><description>
France's attacking trio - Kylian Mbappé, Ousmane Dembélé and Michael Olise - have dominated the World Cup headlines, scoring plenty of goals and dazzling fans with skilful moves and fast breaks past opposing defences. Meanwhile, at the other end of the pitch, goalkeeper Mike Maignan has laid the foundation that's made all that attacking flair possible.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/893e5570-7ec9-11f1-ab90-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mike-maignan.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/893e5570-7ec9-11f1-ab90-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mike-maignan.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">35685f0e-7ebf-11f1-b200-5581fa219da1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:53:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/893e5570-7ec9-11f1-ab90-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mike-maignan.jpg">AFP - JEWEL SAMAD</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine's allies gather in Paris as Kremlin dismisses 'coalition of warmongers'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-ukraine-s-allies-gather-in-paris-as-kremlin-dismisses-coalition-of-warmongers</link><description>
Allies of Ukraine gathered in Paris on Monday alongside President Volodymyr Zelensky to reaffirm their support for Kyiv and step up pressure on Russia, at a summit of the so-called "Coalition of the Willing" that the Kremlin promptly dismissed as a meeting of leaders who "do not want peace".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c048ec60-7e88-11f1-b680-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98RE6CT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c048ec60-7e88-11f1-b680-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98RE6CT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48600820-7e95-11f1-94fb-79dafa8f9333</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:46:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c048ec60-7e88-11f1-b680-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-98RE6CT.jpg">AFP - HANDOUT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France to summon Russian ambassador over cyber attacks</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-france-to-summon-russian-ambassador-over-cyber-attacks-as-eu-imposes-sanctions</link><description>
France will summon the Russian ambassador to Paris over an alleged Russian cyberhacking campaign against European countries including France, as the EU and Britain targeted Russia with coordinated sanctions. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e478ee8-7ea1-11f1-824b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T082209Z-700640867-RC2M3LAVNOCA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e478ee8-7ea1-11f1-824b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T082209Z-700640867-RC2M3LAVNOCA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa43c21a-7ea0-11f1-9bd8-d560f093ee90</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:06:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e478ee8-7ea1-11f1-824b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T082209Z-700640867-RC2M3LAVNOCA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-FRANCE.jpg">© Alice Sacco/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Record 128 migrants cross Channel in one boat as overall numbers drop</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-record-128-migrants-cross-channel-in-one-boat-even-as-overall-numbers-drop</link><description>
A small boat carrying 128 people has reached the coast of England, marking a new record for the largest single crossing of the Channel on a small boat, even as the number of crossings has dropped in recent months.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6ad9c5e-5e51-11f1-b870-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-23T112320Z-1587055107-RC2TELAIYLCQ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-MIGRATION-FRANCE-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6ad9c5e-5e51-11f1-b870-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-23T112320Z-1587055107-RC2TELAIYLCQ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-MIGRATION-FRANCE-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4676965a-7e9a-11f1-b6e4-efef7f7c984b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 09:57:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6ad9c5e-5e51-11f1-b870-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-23T112320Z-1587055107-RC2TELAIYLCQ-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-MIGRATION-FRANCE-BRITAIN.jpg">© Dylan Martinez/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Experts to deliver verdict on EU social media controls for children</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-experts-to-deliver-verdict-on-eu-social-media-controls-for-children</link><description>
An expert committee is due to deliver its recommendations on Monday on how the European Union should regulate children's access to social media, including a potential blanket ban. More than 20 countries worldwide, including France, have already implemented or proposed age restrictions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8b57e38-f9ee-11f0-b804-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-82KW3GN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8b57e38-f9ee-11f0-b804-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-82KW3GN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4d90148-7dd6-11f1-a90a-4126f2da51c4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:35:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b8b57e38-f9ee-11f0-b804-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-82KW3GN.jpg">© AFP - DAVID GRAY </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Massive fire burns in Fontainebleau near Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260713-massive-fire-burns-in-fontainebleau-near-paris</link><description>
Firefighers are mobilised in the Fontainebleau forest south of Paris to contain a major fire that started Sunday and has since forced the evacuation of residents in the area and shut down a major highway at the start of a busy summer holiday travel weekend.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/91d8dbec-7e83-11f1-bfbe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T210510Z-2118620046-RC2KCMA9N2WS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/91d8dbec-7e83-11f1-bfbe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T210510Z-2118620046-RC2KCMA9N2WS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7d3c358-7e83-11f1-8358-9de93d8b8c57</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:35:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/91d8dbec-7e83-11f1-bfbe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T210510Z-2118620046-RC2KCMA9N2WS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Benoit Tessier/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Trump lifts Turkey sanctions, eyes F-35 sale</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260713-trump-lifts-turkey-sanctions-eyes-f-35-sale</link><description>
US President Donald Trump made headlines this week at the Nato summit in Ankara by declaring an end to all sanctions against Turkey, paving the way for the sale of the F-35 stealth fighter jet to the alarm of Greece and Israel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13d2c946-7ea2-11f1-832c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08t165506z-1517548943-rc2s9magdwgg-rtrmadp-3-nato-summit-trump.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/13d2c946-7ea2-11f1-832c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08t165506z-1517548943-rc2s9magdwgg-rtrmadp-3-nato-summit-trump.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d2c9f5c-7ea4-11f1-a02f-d560f093ee90</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 10:19:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Spain braced to face France's firepower in World Cup semi-final</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260712-final-before-final-france-face-spain-in-world-cup-blockbuster</link><description>
Spain will attempt to neutralise one of the most potent attacking arsenals in World Cup history on Tuesday when they take on France in a heavyweight semi-final showdown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5fa02d0-7e3c-11f1-9501-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/5b4980ddae19f1b31d745915665fffdfd3226025.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5fa02d0-7e3c-11f1-9501-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/5b4980ddae19f1b31d745915665fffdfd3226025.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6c385f6-7e3c-11f1-b6e6-23db90b33098</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:58:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5fa02d0-7e3c-11f1-9501-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/5b4980ddae19f1b31d745915665fffdfd3226025.jpg">© Odd ANDERSEN / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>China's missile test overshadowed by Iran war, but Pacific nations are watching</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260713-china-s-missile-test-overshadowed-by-iran-war-but-pacific-nations-are-watching</link><description>
China recenly test-fired a nuclear-capable missile from a submarine into the Pacific, the first such launch from a nuclear-powered vessel and the first submarine-based test since 1982.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9974988c-7b9a-11f1-9a4c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Jin-Type-094-Class-Ballistic-Missile-Submarine.jfif"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9974988c-7b9a-11f1-9a4c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Jin-Type-094-Class-Ballistic-Missile-Submarine.jfif" type="" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5720654-7b9a-11f1-85a0-5b9af79f737d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 08:05:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France remembers 'old demons' of antisemitism on first annual Dreyfus day</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-france-remembers-old-demons-of-antisemitism-on-first-annual-dreyfus-day</link><description>
Sunday saw France observe its first annual day of commemoration for Alfred Dreyfus, a Jewish army officer wrongly convicted of treason in one of the country's most notorious cases of antisemitism. With reports of hate speech on the rise, President Emmanuel Macron said France had yet to shed its "old demons" of prejudice.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21a8c7dc-7d3a-11f1-84f6-9f5186b7b518</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:44:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg">© AFP - THOMAS SAMSON </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>In Zimbabwe, community seed banks are reviving indigenous crops</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260712-in-zimbabwe-community-seed-banks-are-reviving-indigenous-crops</link><description>
Zimbabwean farmers are reviving drought-resistant traditional crops through a community seed bank, helping them cope with worsening climate variability. The initiative, rooted in indigenous knowledge, is strengthening food security and offering a safety net against future droughts and floods.
